# Plan Mode — granular todos

When in **Plan Mode**, calling **CreatePlan**, or producing an implementation plan before coding:

1. Read and follow [`ai/skills/implementation-planning/SKILL.md`](ai/skills/implementation-planning/SKILL.md).
2. Every plan MUST include structured frontmatter `todos` with `id` and `content` (not prose-only task lists).
3. Each `content` MUST include at least one **repo-relative file path** and a **concrete action** (type, method, or migration name when known).
4. Split coarse items until an implementation agent can execute without codebase search.
5. Always end with a **`verify`** todo naming exact `dotnet build`, unit `dotnet test` csproj, then integration `dotnet test` csproj **last** when Infrastructure criteria apply ([`ai/skills/implementation-planning/SKILL.md`](ai/skills/implementation-planning/SKILL.md)).
6. For each **behavior** change, pair todos **`{name}-test-red`** then **`{name}-impl`**. See [`ai/skills/test-driven-development/SKILL.md`](ai/skills/test-driven-development/SKILL.md).

Do not finalize or present a plan for approval while todos remain vague. Do not place `*-impl` behavior todos before the matching `*-test-red` todo.
